# Line endings are LF everywhere, decided by the repository rather than by
# whoever cloned it.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its *system* config — invisible
# to `git config --global --get` — so a Windows clone checks every file out as
# CRLF. Prettier writes LF, so `pnpm format:check` then fails on essentially
# every file in the repo. That failure reads like a formatting problem and is
# not one, which makes it expensive to diagnose exactly once per contributor.
#
# It is not only cosmetic: a shell script checked out with CRLF fails to execute
# on Linux, because the kernel reads the carriage return as part of the
# interpreter path. `scripts/session-start.sh` runs as a hook.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated, and diffed byte-for-byte by CI check 4.
packages/db/src/database.types.ts text eol=lf

# Never transform these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated by `pnpm baml:generate`, and diffed byte-for-byte by CI check 2.
packages/prompts/baml_client/** text eol=lf
